# Security Policy

## Project Status

**MediAssist AI** is a hackathon prototype (v1.0) built for the AI for Bharat Hackathon 2026.  
It uses **synthetic data only** and is not intended for production or clinical use.

---

## Supported Versions

| Version | Supported          | Notes |
|---------|--------------------|-------|
| 1.0.x   | ✅ | Current — hackathon prototype |
| < 1.0   | ❌ | Pre-release builds |

---

## Security Architecture

| Layer | Protection |
|-------|-----------|
| Data in transit | TLS 1.3 via API Gateway + HTTPS |
| Data at rest | AWS S3 + DynamoDB default encryption |
| Access control | IAM roles with least-privilege policies |
| API | AWS API Gateway with CORS restrictions |
| No real PHI | Synthetic data only — no patient records |

---

## Known Limitations (Prototype)

- No authentication or user login system
- No rate limiting on API endpoints
- EC2 Ollama endpoint is not behind VPC
- Not HIPAA certified — designed to be HIPAA-aligned for demo only
- Not suitable for processing real patient data under any circumstances

---

## Reporting a Vulnerability

If you discover a security vulnerability in this project:

1. **Do not** open a public GitHub issue
2. Email the team lead directly: **Bhavik Patel** — contact via GitHub profile
3. Include:
   - Description of the vulnerability
   - Steps to reproduce
   - Potential impact

**Response time**: We aim to respond within 48 hours and provide a fix or workaround within 7 days.

---

## Responsible Disclosure

We follow responsible disclosure principles:
- We will acknowledge your report promptly
- We will keep you updated on the fix progress
- We will credit you in release notes if you wish

---

## Disclaimer

> This system is a **demonstration prototype** built for educational and hackathon purposes.  
> It must **not** be used in any clinical, diagnostic, or production healthcare environment.  
> Always consult qualified healthcare professionals for medical decisions.

